# Pairwise quality model

For repeated comparisons, maintain a latent quality model.

Simple version:

```python
quality_delta = mean(child_axis_score - parent_axis_score)
quality_delta_lcb = empirical_bernstein_lcb(deltas)
```

Better version:

```text
P(child beats parent on task i, axis a)
    = sigmoid(θ_child,a - θ_parent,a - β_i,a)
```

where:

```text
θ = runtime capability on axis
β = task difficulty
```

This is an IRT-style model.

Promotion uses:

```text
LCB(θ_child,a - θ_parent,a) > δ_a
```

For open-ended pairwise preference, use a Bradley-Terry/Davidson model:

```text
P(child wins) = exp(θ_child) / (exp(θ_child) + exp(θ_parent) + tie_mass)
```

Again:

```text
child promoted only if lower-bound preference delta clears threshold
```

