# Capability archive vs release archive

Another correction: not every useful improvement is deployable.

Use two archives.

```text
Capability archive:
    Stores candidates that improve a capability axis.
    Candidate may still be imperfect.
    Used for continued evolution.

Release archive:
    Stores candidates that pass release gates.
    Used for export/deployment.
```

This matters because a candidate that improves from 40% to 70% on a hard frontier is valuable for evolution even if it is not yet production-safe.

But only safety-clean candidates enter the capability archive.

```text
Safety hard gates:
    no eval leakage
    no forbidden file access
    no sandbox escape
    schema valid
    no tamper

Release hard gates:
    all required user-facing correctness gates pass
```

So:

```python
if safety_clean and quality_delta_lcb > δ:
    capability_archive.insert(child)

if release_gates_pass and quality_delta_lcb > δ:
    release_archive.insert(child)
```

This allows real hill-climbing.

